{"case_id":"C035","gap_exists":true,"gap_type":["entry_point","attack_surface"],"commit_induced":"NO","maintenance_needed":false,"confidence":99,"affected_functions":["hasher.update!","hasher.update_u32!","hasher.up!","hasher.up_x86_sse42!"],"reason":"H0 exclusively exercises JSON decoding through fuzz_cpp, fuzz_complex, fuzz_simple, wuffs_aux::DecodeJson, and wuffs_json__decoder__decode_tokens; it never invokes the xxhash32 hasher entry points. That leaves S1's hasher.update!, hasher.update_u32!, and hasher.up! outside H0's reachable attack surface. However, the same gap existed in S0: H0 also did not reach hasher.update!, hasher.update_u32!, hasher.up!, or the former hasher.up_x86_sse42! path. The commit removes the x86 SSE4.2 specialization and makes hasher.up! non-choosy without adding an entry point, protocol, state, configuration, or input-semantic requirement. It therefore does not introduce or materially aggravate the harness gap.","evidence":["H0 defines WUFFS_CONFIG__MODULE__JSON and WUFFS_CONFIG__MODULE__AUX__JSON, but no XXHASH32 module.","H0 calls wuffs_json__decoder__decode_tokens in fuzz_complex and fuzz_simple and wuffs_aux::DecodeJson in fuzz_cpp; no hasher identifier appears in its execution paths.","S0 already routed hasher.update! through hasher.up! and optionally selected hasher.up_x86_sse42!, none of which H0 invoked.","S1 deletes hasher.up_x86_sse42!, removes choose up = [up_x86_sse42], and changes hasher.up! from choosy to a regular private function while preserving the public hasher.update! and hasher.update_u32! entry points."],"recommended_action":"No commit-specific harness maintenance is needed. A separate xxhash32 harness could address the pre-existing coverage gap, but it is not required by this commit."}
